{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgF8XMDDp6AdZYBTzk4VQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"prompt\": \"A square abstract painting that fills the entire image edge to edge, with no frame, wall, room, or gallery setting. Purely nonrepresentational: no recognizable objects, figures, faces, bodies, scenes, landscapes, horizons, machines, diagrams, symbols, icons, letters, numbers, or text. Ground: a deep indigo-black field, slightly uneven, as if the canvas was rubbed back in places. Palette: cold ultramarine and teal running against a burnt-orange ember and a thin streak of pale ochre, with a few small patches of off-white. Composition: a dense, tangled knot of layered strokes sits slightly off-center in the upper left, built from many translucent passes that thicken into impasto and then thin into scraped, dry-brush veils. A taut diagonal current of rapid, sweeping gestures runs from the lower right toward the knot, creating spatial tension and a sense of rhythm, with a few strokes that break off mid-motion. Surround the knot with broad areas of empty, lightly textured ground so the density has room to breathe. Brushwork: varied, from loaded palette-knife drags and dripping lines to soft, feathered glazes and fingerprint-like smudges. Texture: a mix of gritty pigment, glossy wet-looking passages, and matte scumbled areas. Contrast: strong value shifts where the ember color meets the indigo, with the lightest notes placed sparingly near the center. The overall mood is restless and searching, with dense energy concentrated in one area and quiet, open space around it.\"}"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":442,"cache_read_input_tokens":15292,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":442},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"